riscv64 zkVM: fixed locals are not pinned

The uGC never moves objects, so a pinned (`fixed`) local need not be pinned: pinned locals
cannot be enregistered and are zero-initialized in the prolog and cleared after use. With
JitZkNoPinning (default 0; bflat passes 1 for the zkVM libcs) the attribute is dropped at
import for the root method's and inlinees' locals, and the pointer lives in a register.
Measured with perf-60 on nine blocks: -0.17% executed steps, identical outputs.

diff --git a/src/coreclr/jit/importer.cpp b/src/coreclr/jit/importer.cpp
index f75974de2..21b9e96cb 100644
--- a/src/coreclr/jit/importer.cpp
+++ b/src/coreclr/jit/importer.cpp
@@ -14434,7 +14434,11 @@ unsigned Compiler::impInlineFetchLocal(unsigned lclNum DEBUGARG(const char* reas
         // Copy over key info
         lvaTable[tmpNum].lvType                 = lclTyp;
         lvaTable[tmpNum].lvHasLdAddrOp          = inlineeLocal.lclHasLdlocaOp;
+#if defined(TARGET_RISCV64)
+        lvaTable[tmpNum].lvPinned = inlineeLocal.lclIsPinned && (JitConfig.JitZkNoPinning() == 0);
+#else
         lvaTable[tmpNum].lvPinned               = inlineeLocal.lclIsPinned;
+#endif
         lvaTable[tmpNum].lvHasILStoreOp         = inlineeLocal.lclHasStlocOp;
         lvaTable[tmpNum].lvHasMultipleILStoreOp = inlineeLocal.lclHasMultipleStlocOp;
 
